<wpf:ResourceDictionary xml:space="preserve" xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml" xmlns:s="clr-namespace:System;assembly=mscorlib" xmlns:ss="urn:shemas-jetbrains-com:settings-storage-xaml" xmlns:wpf="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation">
  <!--
    Team-shared InspectCode / ReSharper severity profile for the
    ConsoleAppTemplate solution.

    Scope: this solution is the `dotnet new cwconsole` TEMPLATE CONTENT — a
    scaffold users receive and edit. InspectCode's "unused member" family
    fires on scaffolding whose real consumer is the user's code (not the
    solution), so those rules are silenced solution-wide rather than case-
    by-case:

      * NotAccessedField.Compiler        — 38 palette constants in
        Framework/ConsoleColors.cs. The palette exists so the generated app
        can call `ConsoleColors.Foreground.Red` etc. from any command the
        user adds; the template itself does not consume every entry.

      * UnusedAutoPropertyAccessor.Global — Model/SampleConfiguration.cs
        `CommandTimeout` (and any future settings the user adds). The
        setter is invoked by Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration binding
        via reflection, which InspectCode cannot see.

      * RedundantUsingDirective           — Program.cs `using
        ConsoleAppTemplate.Command;`. The generated Program.cs ships with
        every project-namespace `using` in place so a user adding a new
        subcommand or explicit [Subcommand(typeof(...))] entry does not
        need to reason about which imports to add. Intentional
        scaffolding, not dead code.

    Sibling templates (SubCommandTemplate / EtlSubCommandTemplate) carry
    {DefaultNamespace} placeholder tokens and are not in this solution, so
    they are not inspected here.
  -->
  <s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=NotAccessedField_002ECompiler/@EntryIndexedValue">DO_NOT_SHOW</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=UnusedAutoPropertyAccessor_002EGlobal/@EntryIndexedValue">DO_NOT_SHOW</s:String>
  <s:String x:Key="/Default/CodeInspection/Highlighting/InspectionSeverities/=RedundantUsingDirective/@EntryIndexedValue">DO_NOT_SHOW</s:String>
</wpf:ResourceDictionary>
